!Sample_treatment_protocol_ch1 = The assay of transposase accessible chromatin (ATAC-seq) uses hyperactive Tn5 transposase to simultaneously cut and ligate adapters for high-throughput sequencing at regions of increased accessibility.
!Sample_treatment_protocol_ch1 = we treated sgControl or sgCop1-transduced 4T1 cells with vehicle control or 20ng/ml IFNγ for 24 hrs
!Sample_molecule_ch1 = genomic DNA
!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = ATAC-seq was performed on replicates (200,000 cells) by the Center for Functional Cancer Epigenetics at DFCI as previously described.
!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = Genome-wide mapping of insertion ends by high-throughput sequencing allows for multidimensional assays of the regulatory landscape of chromatin with a relatively simple protocol.
!Sample_data_processing = Sequenced reads were trimmed for adaptor sequence, and then mapped to mm10 whole genome using BWA using the default parameters.
!Sample_data_processing = We used MACS2 for peak calling.
